    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25KWiJPRkGcgDQT8pc4YUMR)_\n\n## What\n- `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` (`C-c w b l`) and `sp-bibtex-lint-convert` (`C-c w b L`) now work on one `.bib` file:\n  - the file of the current buffer when it is a `.bib` file\n  - otherwise, or with a prefix argument, one picked with completion from `sp-bibtex-files`\n- The dry run uses the shared `sp-batch-report` buffer from #351 (the `vulpea-doctor`-style report):\n  - each entry links to its line (`RET` visits, `n`/`p` move, `g` refreshes)\n  - it never changes a file\n- `convert` shows the rewrites in batches:\n  - batch size is the new `sp-bibtex-lint-batch-size`, default 50\n  - for each batch you answer `a` apply, `s` skip or `q` quit; the next batch is shown only after the answer\n  - nothing is written without an `a`\n  - the file is copied to `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory` before the first write, and written again after each applied batch\n  - it refuses when the open buffer of the file is unsaved, or when the file changed on disk after the lint\n- The rewrite itself is unchanged (names to `Last, First`, field order). Duplicate keys, names near an author note and entries with a comment inside are reported only.\n- The old `sp-bibtex-lint-report-mode` and `sp-bibtex-lint-visit` are gone, replaced by the shared mode.\n- Literate doc (`docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org`) updated as bullet lists; it tangles to the committed `sp-bibprocess.el`.\n\n## Tests\n- 12 tests in `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el`, all pass in Emacs 29 with `sp-cache-dir` and `sp-var-dir` defined: file choice, results, apply, batches of 2 and the default 50 (50 + 50 + 20), nothing written or backed up without an apply, unsaved buffer, file changed on disk, report links.\n- Not run on the real `.bib` files or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule. The branch is not prefixed with the PR number, because the session's branch name was fixed.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCsguMS2m92TG5VLGt)_",
